  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nThis Weekend: Dry and quiet weather expected with gusty west \nwinds will persist into the afternoon. A Lake Wind Advisory runs \ntill 5PM tonight with wave heights as high as 5 feet at times. A \ncold front will arrive overnight brining additional gusty winds \nduring the day tomorrow. In addition most CAMs are siting a \nsystem of light rain/snow showers moving NW to SE across the \nnortheastern half of the CWA. The QPF with these showers should \nnot amount to much at all through with light sprinkles or flurries\npossible depending on the timing of the passage. CAMs do vary in \nthe 6 hour passage timing of these showers.\n\nMonday onward: With the breakdown of a weak ridge a slightly SW \ntilt will enter the zonal flow. Ensemble runs are going back and \nforth as to whether to include scattered light snow showers with \nthe entrance of this feature from forecast to forecast. Regardless,\nQPF won't be much of anything here. Flow returns to zonal with \ndry conditions and near normal temps for highs and above normal \ntemps for low. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & NBM DEVIATIONS:\n\nNo changes to NBM this cycle. No changes to PoPs, since the\ncurrent spatial extent of PoPs mirrors the CAMs well. Though\nuncertainty remains, the impacts of precipitation remains low.\n\nConfidence is HIGH through Sunday night.\n\nConfidence is MODERATE from Monday onward.",
